  "row_count": 21,
  "notes": {
    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nPhase change: 1337.58 K, melting point of Au; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 2.957$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 8.920 + 0.012 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.387 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.920\\times10^{-3}T+0.006\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.387\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.790$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1337.58 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = 39.845 - 0.661 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.914 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 23.350 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 39.845 + 0.661 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.914 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 11.675 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 30.204 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n1337.58-2000 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 38.970 - 3.224 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.154 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 4.550 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 38.970 + 3.224 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.154 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 2.275 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 46.979 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Mills (80) who estimated all except enthalpy of formation at 298 K. ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated.",
